m-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the members test investigation to a subagent while I look at the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` runs 16 tests with no failures. At first only 15 tests ran, because `tests/test_search.py` couldn't be imported. I didn't change any tests.\n\nI fixed six bugs in `catalog/`:\n\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` kept the year as a string, so `age()` crashed when subtracting it. It now converts the year to a number with `int(year)`.\n- **`factory.py`**: `sample_books()` was missing `Emma`. Its own description lists three titles, and the tests expect all three.\n- **`fees.py`**: the late fee was days *plus* the daily rate, so one day late cost 1.25. It now multiplies days by the 0.25 daily rate.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n`, and an empty list if `n` is 0 or less.\n- **`members.py`**: the borrowing limit was set to 3, but the comment beside it says five and so do the tests. I changed it to 5. A subagent looked into this test file and found the cause.\n- **`search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports it from `catalog.text`, where the function is defined.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 6, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 95376, "requests_cache_write": 78628, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5117512000